    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1197-a5">

                <pb facs="0968" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg852"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5—Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Commander Kavanagh to Consul Alger</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>U. S. S. “<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Annapolis</hi>,”</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 23, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Please remind General Muñoz that: Protection not protests is what is desired
                    here; the protests can be settled afterwards. For more than ten days now the
                    Americans here have been without protection from the Mexicans although the
                    deplorable state of affairs has been repeatedly brought to their attention.</p>
                <p>I would like to know definitely if General Muñoz refuses protection on the
                    grounds that armed men were landed from the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Annapolis</hi> or if that is not the reason, what is the reason he does not
                    send a force here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kavanagh.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
